(A text read from the arguments or the environment is appended to a buffer like any other text)
a buffer called holder is 256 bytes in size.
a text called 'the binary name' is arguments's name.
append 'the binary name' to holder.
If holder's length is greater than 0 then, Print "the name was appended".
clear holder.

a text called opening is arguments's first.
a text called following is arguments's second.
a text called closing is arguments's last.
a text called positioned is the argument at 1.
append opening to holder.
append following to holder.
append closing to holder.
append positioned to holder.
Print holder.

a text called home is environment's "HOME".
a text called 'first setting' is environment's first.
clear holder.
append home to holder.
append 'first setting' to holder.
If holder's length is greater than 0 then, Print "the environment was appended".

To 'append the name' with a buffer called gathered.
    a text called 'own name' is arguments's name.
    append 'own name' to gathered.

clear holder.
'append the name' of holder.
If holder's length is greater than 0 then, Print "appended inside a function".
